# Everything the image does not need, and some things it must not have.
#
# .git is the important line. A build does not need the repository's history, and
# copying it into a layer ships every branch name, commit message and author address to
# anyone who pulls the image.
.git
.github

bin/
coverage.out

# Python and Node working directories. examples/demo-app/.venv alone is tens of
# megabytes of build context that would be uploaded to the daemon on every build.
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/node_modules

# Local environment files. A KEK or a database password reaching a layer is exactly the
# accident this file exists to prevent.
.env
*.env
deploy/.env
